# What an install receives is `git archive` of a commit, which is also GitHub's ZIP. Files an
# agent never reads in a session stay in the repository but out of that package, which keeps
# the skill under the upload's 200-file limit (issue #80). Clones still carry everything.
# `python tooling/skill/verify_skill.py --package` checks the package these rules produce.
.gitattributes      export-ignore
.gitignore          export-ignore
.github/            export-ignore
docs/               export-ignore
REMAINING_WORK.md   export-ignore
tooling/**/tests/   export-ignore
